# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
#
# Controller input for 007 - Agent Under Fire (SLES-50539), from power-on: what
# a player presses to get from the first screens into the game, as a script
# for ps2n-host -pad (scripts/windows/game.ps1 -Pad). The frame numbers are
# those of a run with no memory card in either slot.
#
# This file holds button presses, written for PS2Native's tests. Nothing in
# it comes from the game. What each press is for was found by looking at the
# pictures of runs under stock PCSX2 (scripts/windows/sheets.ps1).
#
# frame  input  frames held

# "Language Selection": English, the first, is chosen.
300     cross   4
# The EA and MGM logos, then the intro film from about frame 1100: skip it
# (at frame 1200 it does not take the button yet).
1700    cross   4
# "memory card (8MB) (for PlayStation 2) is not inserted ... Do you want to
# start?" from about frame 2150, No drawn as chosen: to Yes, and Yes.
2500    left    4
2600    cross   4
# The title screen from about frame 2650, "Press START button" (left alone
# about 30 seconds, it plays the intro film again).
3100    start   4
# The main menu from about frame 3150: Select Mission (the first, chosen).
3300    cross   4
# "Select Mission" from about frame 3400: the first, "Trouble in Paradise".
3500    cross   4
# The mission's briefing from about frame 3600, four pages: Continue past each.
3700    cross   4
3800    cross   4
3900    cross   4
4000    cross   4
